  "disclaimer_extra": "Whataburger publishes each ingredient with its own weight and each menu item as a recipe of those ingredients, so every figure here is their arithmetic on their numbers -- the same sum their own app makes. It reproduces what they print: a Whataburger comes to 589.5 against a published 590. Their recipes also count the seasoned oil the buns are griddled in, which is not something you order, so a burger you build here runs a few calories under the same one on the menu.",
  "glyph": "burger",
  "formats": [
   "Burger",
   "Chicken",
   "Breakfast"
  ],
  "blurb": "Whataburger is composed from parts more completely than any other chain here: it publishes a weight and a full label for every ingredient, down to a single 15-gram tomato slice, and builds its own menu by counting them. That means you can add a third slice of cheese and get a number Whataburger would agree with."
 },
